3 STAE Oppland
3 CTRY Norway
1 OCCU Byfogd, sorenskriver, eidsvollsmann, stortingsrepresentant, odelstingspresident, amtmann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.snl.no/.nbl_biografi/Lauritz_Weidemann/utdypning http://www.snl.no/Riksforsamlingen/Riksforsamlingen_p%C3%A5_Eidsvoll_1814
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Lars Christophersen Weidemann, sheriff in Nedenes fogderie, and Marie Sommerfelt. Weidemann was 16 December 1797 married Marie Qvist Ditlevine from Sandstø at Arendal (born May 22, 1774, death at Steinberg March 
2 CONC 18, 1866). They had ten children, four of whom died young. Weide Manns daughters were never married, allegedly because her father could not accept any of the candidates spouse. This is enough background for the local tradition tha
2 CONC t inspired the family Camilla Collett to write Amtmandens Døtre. One of Lauritz Weide Manns brothers were Christopher Christian Weidemann.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] senior official
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauritz Weidemann was a student in 1790 and achieved the degree cand Juris in 1793. He was byfogd, byskriver mm in Rakaia in 1797, sorenskriver of Southern Sunnmøre 12 December 1798 and sorenskriver of Toten, Ballarat and Vardal 1
2 CONC  October 1802 3. February 1817 he was Amtmannens in Hedemarkens County; in Kristians County from 23 August 1821. This last office he retained for 30 years, to 1851, and he was also known as Amtmannens Weidemann.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Politicians
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1814, he was a member of the National Assembly at Eidsvoll, where he quit to the Falsenske party. Weidemann also wrote a draft constitution. In 1814 he was stortingsmann, and he would sit there in the periods 1814-1816, 1827, 1
2 CONC 828, 1836, 1837 and 1839. Weidemann was in the period 1815-1818 member of lovkomiteen, 1818-1822 chairman of the hovedmatrikuleringskommisjonen, 1814-1823 by the Commission regarding the construction of a township in Gujarat. In t
2 CONC he 1815-1816, he was president of Odel Licensing, Vice President of the Storting, the secretary of Parliament and a member of a number of committees. In 1827, he was Storting in 1836 and president in Løgting. He was a member of ak
2 CONC sjonskomiteen under national law 1815-1816 and a member of the national court in 1836.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] Amtmannsgarden Steinberg
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1804 he bought the garden Steinberg, that uncle, sorenskriver Fredrik Sommerfeldt, had begun to build up as the official farm in 1791. Weidemann had listed several new houses in the garden, and he built the garden of a park in 
2 CONC the English landscape style. On the farm he created a private plot for himself and his family. The property came in 1934 in Toten Museums own and is now part of Mjøs museum.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Edit] See also
2 CONT
2 CONT Amundgård, Arne: About family tomb where he was buried in Stenberg, in årboka Totnes 1995, p. 42-49.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruun, Magne: Norwegian gardens through thousands of years, Oslo 2007.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hårstad Sveen, Rune: "1802-1902. 100 years of Weidemann in Stenberg", in årboka Totnes 2002, p. 24-55.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fløystad, Ingeborg: The King's jurisdiction. A study for four draft constitution. Hovedoppgave in history, University of Bergen in 1967.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fløystad, Ingeborg: Sorenskriver Lauritz Weide Manns draft constitution in 1814, in årboka Totnes 1988, p. 11-21.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mannsåker, Dagfinn: Lauritz Weidemann. Biography biografisk the Norwegian Encyclopedia I, Oslo 1977.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mannsåker, Dagfinn and Sætra, Gustav: Lauritz Weidemann. Biography of the Norwegian biografisk Encyclopedia II, Oslo 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT Middle Haug, Leif: Lauritz Weidemann, biography in Totens bygdebok II, p. 353-354.
2 CONT
2 CONT NSDs politician archive: Lauritz Weidemann
2 CONT
2 CONT Sørheim, Ingeborg: Stenberg park. A Danish-Norwegian official garden, 1750-1850. Master's thesis in art history, University of Oslo in 2007.
2 CONT
