1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her blir han omtalt i USA som eksentrisk
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wisconsinhistory.org/Records/Newspaper/BA11117
2 CONT _____________
2 CONT
2 CONT * About 1873, he come north from Chicago and settled at the "Frydenland" cabin at Swamp Creek, a farm and trading post near the Town of Nashville in Forest County, Wis.
2 CONT * 1878-1888, ran the post office named Frydenland ,located in his cabin.
2 CONT * 1885-1899 Forest County Treasurer.
2 CONT * 1899 moved to Pelican Lake area and engaged in land speculation
2 CONT * 1899 moved to Pratt Junction and rented a building to run a general store.
2 CONT * 1901 he purchased a store in Pelican Lake and operated it until 1911
2 CONT * 1912 Moved to British Columbia
2 CONT * 1913 Moved to Odanah, on the Bad River Reservation near Ashland, where Kate had moved when Motzfeldt retired from the store business.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1848 - Norway
2 CONT * Parents:	Carl Frederik Motzfeldt, Emilie Marie Erneste Motzfeldt (born Birch)
2 CONT * Wife:	Kate Ne-suw-we-ge-zhic-go-quay Motzfeldt
2 CONT * Children:	Emma "Wi ni ba go bo kwe" Ackley (born Dinesen), Wa- Bish- Ka Motzfeldt, Jennie Motzfeldt
2 CONT * Siblings:	Peter Motzfeldt, Carl Frederik Motzfeldt, Anna Pauline Erneste Motzfeldt, Erneste Motzfeldt, Arthur Carlsen Motzfeldt
