1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Kilder==
2 CONT
2 CONT SAK, Arendal sokneprestkontor, Trefoldighet, F/Fa/L0008: Ministerialbok nr. A 8, 1878-1899, s. 76.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20060207040084 Født 23. april 1886 (døpt 20. juni 1886) i Arendal] - «Helge Johan» (nr. 32).
2 CONT ----
2 CONT SAO, Østre Bærum prestekontor Kirkebøker, F/Fa/L0001: Ministerialbok nr. 1, 1905-1924, s. 249.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20061123310897 Død 7. juli 1924 på Granheim sanatorium, Follebu, Gausdal] [se anmerkning ytterst til høyre], gravlagt 12. juli 1924 på Vestre gravlund, Oslo - «enkemand Dr. phil. Helge Gjessing, Ko
2 CONC nservator ved universitetet, arkæolog» (løpenr. 0, dvs. gravlagt i annet sogn).
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''''''Helge Johan Gjessing (23 April 1886 – 4 July 1924) was a Norwegian archaeologist.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Arendal as a son of philologist Gustav Antonio Gjessing[1] and his wife Helga Monrad. He was a grandson of Marcus Jacob Monrad,[2] a first cousin of Harald Gjessing, and through his brother, the vicar Marcus Jacob G
2 CONC jessing, he was an uncle of archaeologist Gutorm Gjessing. In December 1913 he married Thale Sandvig, from Lillehammer (1890–1918), a daughter of professor Anders Sandvig.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He enrolled as a student of history and archaeology in 1904, and graduated with the cand.philol. degree in 1912.[1] He was hired as curator at Stavanger Museum in 1913, and was promoted to director in 1914. He worked as subdirecto
2 CONC r at the Royal Frederick University from 1917. In 1920 he took the dr.philos. degree with the thesis Rogalands stenalder, about the Stone Age in Rogaland. He died at a sanatorium in Gausdal in July 1924. http://en.wikipedia.org/wi
2 CONC ki/Helge_Gjessing
