1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cause of Death: Shock & induries caused by being ru n over by fright train. Died at the age of 26 yrs., 4 months, 2 days Buried April 16, 1914 in Mt. Olive, Cemetery. Chicago, IL Obit as printed : Chicago Daily Tri
2 CONC bune, Friday, 17 Apr. 19 14, pg. 3 Obituary article, Death-Johnson, Vilma Christine WOMAN WANDERS FROM HOME TO MEET DEATH ON TRACKS Mrs. Zilma Johnson Killed by St. PaulTrain While Husband Ar ranges Funiture in New House. Mrs. Zel
2 CONC ma Johnson wandered away yesterday from the new hom e in which her husband was arranging furniture and threw hersel f under the wheels of a St. Paul switch engines on the elevated track s at North Herman avenue. She was taken to W
2 CONC est Monroe and South Rockw ell streets in the cab of the locomotive and placed in an ambulance. Befor e arrival at the Washington Park hospital she died. Mrs. Johnson was released from the Dunning hospital for th e insane on Sunda
2 CONC y. Since the birth of a child thirteen months ago s he had been morbid and, according to her husband, a nervous wreck. Ther e is another child, 7 years old. The Johnsons were moving into 3446 Potomac avenue, which i s near the rai
2 CONC lroad tracks. Several women neighbors saw Mrs. Johnson wandering about o n the tracks, bun none saw her death, so far as the police coul d learn. (source: Judi Schmidt had the newspaper article)
