1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Lars Andersen Mørch (c. 1707 – 1755)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Andersen Mørch was an underkonstabel (sub-constable) in the garrison artillery, later active as a merchant and farmer in Sandefjord and Østre Aker during the first half of the 18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Origin and Genealogical Context'''
2 CONT * '''Birth''': Estimated c. '''1707 in Sandefjord'''. Direct baptismal records are missing because the local parish register only commences in 1709. While his burial record in 1755 estimates his age at 41 (suggesting a birth c. 17
2 CONC 14), such age declarations in 18th-century garrison registries were notoriously approximate. A birth date of c. 1707 positions him perfectly within the pre-registry lacuna, resolving the contradiction with the Sandefjord books (17
2 CONC 09–1719), which record other children of his presumed parents but omit Lars.
2 CONT * '''Heritage''': According to the reconstruction by Captain G. Mørch, Lars was the son of the shipmaster '''Anders Knudsen Mørch''' (1672–1749) and '''Anne Christine Rosenvold'''. Although S. H. Finne-Grønn (NST IX) expressed pro
2 CONC fessional skepticism due to the lack of a direct baptismal entry, a modern analysis based on **Social Network Analysis (SNA)** strongly validates this lineage. Lars was named after his maternal grandfather, Infantry Captain [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/Lauritz-Rosenvold/6000000007800604458?through=6000000007800466528 Lars (Lauritz) Rosenvold], conforming to the traditional Scandinavian naming custom (*oppkalling*).
2 CONT * '''Historiographical Assessment of the "Aker" Theory''': Finne-Grønn tentatively suggested an alternative hypothesis (p. 337), proposing that Lars might be a brother of a local resident, Mads Andersen Mørch of Aker. However, thi
2 CONC s *argumentum ex silentio* lacks supporting archival evidence. It fails to account for Lars's elite military placement and completely ignores the dense web of documented social, legal, and familial sponsorships connecting Lars to 
2 CONC the Sandefjord-Rosenvold inner circle.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Professional Status and Career'''
2 CONT * '''Military Service''': Lars served as an *underkonstabel* (sub-constable) in the elite Artillery Corps (*Artillerikorpset*), initially in Captain Kiøbing's company in Fredrikshald, and later in Major Barth's company. This speci
2 CONC alized garrison rank required technical and administrative literacy, explaining his distinct social standing within the Akershus Fortress hierarchy and his privilege to be married in the Royal Castle Chapel.
2 CONT * '''Commerce''': In his later years, after relocating to Sagene (Saugene), he transitioned into civilian life, operating as a merchant and farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and Residence'''
2 CONT * '''Marriage''': Married '''Inger Marie Pedersdatter Ringkjøbing''' on 3 Dec 1734 in the Akershus Castle Chapel. 
2 CONT * '''Social Context Analysis''': While Finne-Grønn highlighted the artisan background of the bride's biological father (the tailor-journeyman Peder Ringkjøbing, d. 1720) to question a match with the officer-class Rosenvold lineage
2 CONC , this overlooks the fluid social dynamics of the Akershus garrison. Inger Marie's mother had remarried into the established Bloch household (Mads Jensen Bloch). Intermarriage between specialized garrison military personnel and pr
2 CONC ominent local artisan-merchant families was standard practice. The prestigious venue of the **Royal Castle Chapel** and the elite status of the witnesses further confirm Lars's high social standing.
2 CONT * '''Legal Sponsors (Kautionister)''': A critical legal link is established by his best man (*kautionist*), '''Nicolai Rasmussen Thoer (Thor)''', who was married to Sophie Magdalene Rosenvold (Lars's maternal aunt). Under Danish-N
2 CONC orwegian law, a *kautionist* assumed strict legal and financial liabilities; choosing a maternal uncle-in-law firmly places Lars within the Rosenvold family network.
2 CONT * '''Residential Continuity''': Between 1734 and 1738, Lars and his family resided at '''"Morstuen"''' (Stubberudeie) in Østre Aker. This estate was originally the seat of his maternal grandfather, Captain Lars Rosenvold (d. 1689)
2 CONC . Finne-Grønn noted that Lars lived there merely as a tenant (*inderst*) on church-beneficed land. However, the crucial detail is that he cohabited with '''Anders Pedersen Flor''', the second husband of Lars's maternal grandmother
2 CONC  (Anne Jørgensdatter Melchior). Cohabitation with his grandmother's widower on the grandfather's former estate provides a powerful indicator of hereditary right and family care, completely undermining the notion of a coincidental 
2 CONC tenancy. In 1738, the family relocated to Sagene near Christiania.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children and Evidence''':
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Knud-Mørch/6000000008753149531?through=6000000008754170733 '''Knud Larsen Mørch'''] (1736–1832): Baptized in Aker. He was named after his maternal uncle, Knud Ringkjøbing (d. 1732 in Kurland). Key Ev
2 CONC idence: His godparents included [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Sophia-Knoph-Knoff/6000000217180898822?through=6000000007800466528 Elisabeth Sophie Knoph] (née Rosenvold)—Lars's first cousin—alongside military elites (Offic
2 CONC er P.W. Knoph, Dr. Biernitz), reinforcing the active ties to the Rosenvold family network.
2 CONT # '''Anne Christine Mørch''' (1748–before 1757): Baptized in Aker. Her name serves as a vital genealogical marker, following the strict social convention of naming daughters after their grandmothers—in this case, her paternal gran
2 CONC dmother, [https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Christine-Mørch/6000000002278479974?through=6000000002278479966 Anne Christine Rosenvold] (wife of Anders Mørch).
2 CONT # '''Karen Cathrine Mørch''' (c. 1732 – index).
2 CONT # '''Maren Elisabeth Mørch''' (1740 – index): Born in Fredrikshald during Lars's military deployment.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources & Critical Methodology''':
2 CONT * '''Mørch, G.''': "Familien Mørch: Fra Melsomvik og Smaalenene" [https://slekt1.com/familien-morch-fra-melsomvik-og-smaalenene-1923/ (1923)].
2 CONT * '''Mørch, G.''': "Familien Mørch fra Sandefjord og Larvik", PHT 8. V (1926), [https://www.genealogi.dk/images/pht/1926/1926_8-5-3.pdf pp. 218-234].
2 CONT * '''Finne-Grønn, S. H.''': "Litt om familien Mørch...", NST IX (1944), [https://sporbiblioteket.nb.no/loaderTicket?fid=3330143&type=0&key=6c42f67b83f2bb28c33f97b12e4f18f5 pp. 334-337]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Methodological Note''': While Finne-Grønn’s strictly positivist skepticism regarding the lack of direct baptismal books is noted, his counter-theory fails structural testing. In early 18th-century Norwegian genealogy, where re
2 CONC cords are fragmented, the convergence of property continuity (Morstuen), legally binding family sponsorships (Nicolai Thoer), and military-class socio-economic alignment forms a highly robust, academically sound case for Lars's de
2 CONC scent from the Mørch-Rosenvold lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ———————————
2 CONT
2 CONT HANS LIV og bosted er kun sikkert kjendt mellem 1734 og 1749. Hans fødested og fødselsaar har jeg ikke kunnet finde i nogen kirkebok, mne jeg antar, at han er født i Sandefjord ca. 1707. Stedets første kirkebok begynder først vaar
2 CONC en 1709. Hans dødsaar og begravelsessted kjendes heller ikke. Antagelig har han fra først av været sjømand til i beg.av 1730-aarene, senere gaardbruker og handelsmand i Ø. Aker. Han blev 29de sept. 1734 trolovet paa "Hovedtangen" 
2 CONC ved Akershus befæstninger med Inger Marie Pedersdatter Bloch og viet til hende i Akershus slotskapel 3dje decbr. s.a. Hans kautionist ved trolovelsen var gaardbruker i Ø. Aker Nicoloai Rasmussen Thoer, der var Anders Knudsen Mørch
2 CONC s svoger, og hendes Mads Jensen Bloch, der bodde paa Hovedtangen og vistnok var hendes onkel. - Hendes fødselsaar kjendes heller ikke, da Akers kirkebok for tiden 1689 til og med 1713 er bortkommet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Det bodde som nygifte i "Morstuen" i Ø. Aker, ikke langt fra nuværende Alna Bru's jernbanestation. Den til huset hørende ladebygning gjenstaar endnu. - Stuebygningene eides i 1689 av Anders Knudsen Mørchs svigerfar, infanterikapte
2 CONC in Lars Larsen Rosenvold og i midten av 1730-aarene i forening av Lars Mørch og gaardbruker Anders PEdersen Floer, der hadde været gift med kaptein Rosenvolds enke Annichen Jørgensdatter Mercker. I 1738 blev de begge nødt til at f
2 CONC raflytte huset, hvorefter Lars med familie flyttet til Saugene ved Kristiania, der dengang laa i Ø. Aker. Her bodde han sikkert til henimot 1749. Senere ophører alle sikre oplysninger om ham og hans hustru.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://slekt1.com/familien-morch-fra-melsomvik-og-smaalenene-1923/
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Man kjender ikkedet aar Anders K. Mørch blev gift med Anne Christine Rosenvold, men da hun var født i 1683, er der intet til hinder for, at ægteskabet foregik flere aar før 1709 og at Lars er født mellem 1705 og 1708."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sandeherreds Iste kirkebok først begynder mårs 1709..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: "Familien Mørch fra Sandefjord og Larvik. Af Kommandørkaptajn Gustav Mørch."  https://www.genealogi.dk/images/pht/1926/1926_8-5-3.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Motargumenter. Kilde: Finne-Grønn, Stian Herlofsen, (1869-1953). Litt om familien Mørch fra Melsomvik og Smålenene. NST 9 (1944): 334-337. https://sporbiblioteket.nb.no/loaderTicket?fid=3330143&type=0&key=6c42f67b83f2bb28c33f97b12
2 CONC e4f18f5
2 CONT
