1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Johan Georg (Jørgen) Marichs (1699 – 1739)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Georg Marichs was born in 1699 in Copenhagen, Denmark. He later moved to Norway and settled in Christiania (now Oslo), where he worked as a "vinforlader" (wine steward or cellar manager) for the prominent merchant P. Leuch.
2 CONT
2 CONT On January 23, 1731, he married '''Dorte Bertelsdatter''' (1708–1786) in Christiania. She was the daughter of skipper Bertel Hansøn and Maren Bugge.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT '''Eleonore Lovise Marichs''' (1733–1795). She married master smith Knud Larsen Mørch (1736–1832).
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Marichs died on March 20, 1739, in Christiania at the age of 40. After his death, his widow Dorte remarried in 1740 to Jonas Jonasen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://slaegtsbibliotek.dk/2023/937697.pdf Bugge, Kjeld. Ulrik-slekten Bugge. Oslo, 1948.] P. 24.
