1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Eleonore Louise Movig (1798–1853)'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized in Stokke Church on October 31, 1798. Died of cholera in the outskirts of Fredrikstad on October 6, 1853. Following her second husband's death in 1836, she moved to Fredrikstad with her children.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriages:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Jens Kjøge Movig''' (1798–1821), shipmaster from Nøtterø. Married on January 30, 1821, in Melsomvik; he died shortly after the wedding.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Søren Hansen Movig''' (1794–1836), elder brother of her first husband. Married in 1822.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children (from the second marriage):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Jens Kjøge''' (1822–1837) — died at sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Henrik Ditlev''' (1824–1896) — shipmaster and shipowner at Jeløen, Moss. Married Julie Mathilde Ulsteen.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Anne Marie''' (b. 1826) — married an English engineer; did in Transylvania (Siebenburgen).
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Karen-Tonette-Haus-Howes-Movig/6000000196132465839?through=6000000037133481036 '''Karen Tonette (Antonette)'''] (b. 1829) — married an English engineer; resided in Riga.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Søren Ludvig''' (1832–1905) — shipmaster and shipowner in Fredrikstad.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources:''' 
