1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The children looked forward to spending time visiting Grandma Clara and the aunts and uncles at Thief Lake.  Especially memorable were the Christmas Eves spent there, with the Christmas Gospel from Luke being read.
2 CONC   Christmas songs being sung and the young ones "reciting their pieces" that they had learned for the Sunday School Christmas Program.  We'd usually meet at Aunt Olga's toward supper time and everyone would get into the grain box 
2 CONC on the bob sleds, cuddle under blankets and with the sleigh bells ringing, enjoy the three mile ride across the swamp to th other aunts and uncles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied from the Haugen History Book
2 CONT
2 CONT Clara passed away June 28th 1971 at the age of 98 years and seven months.  She never remarried after the death of Peter 54 years prior.
