1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born Lødingen 1898
2 CONT
2 CONT Graduated from Norway's Institute of Technology
2 CONT
2 CONT Moves to New York in 1924
2 CONT
2 CONT Works as co-engineer for the electrical design of the Wards Island sewage treatment works for new York City, and is the chief electrical engineer with George G. Sharp of New York City. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1933 he exhibited three paintings at the Independent in Grand Central Palace
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1938 he showed two paintings in New York at the Contemporary Arts Gallery, where 1000 artist exhibited two paintings each. Strømsted's two paintings attracted justified attention, resulting in that the director invited him to e
2 CONC xhibit in the New York's famous exhibition lounge.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1940, some of his paintings were shown in Stavanger Art Society, and then in Ålesund, Trondheim and Oslo.
