1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vera was a graduate of Wellesley College, Class of 1949. She's listed in the Who's Who of American Women and was an active member of the national League of American Pen Women, Sarasota Branch, the Wellesley club of
2 CONC  Sarasota, and the Sarasota Art Center. Following in her father's footsteps who once exhibited in the national Gallery of Art in Washington DC, she was herself a longtime artist. She created beautiful art in a variety of forms, fr
2 CONC om driftwood sculptures, to watercolor paintings, photography and art prints, to "Jackson Pollackish" prints on the computer. She last resided in Saraspota Florida, and was a longtime resident of Burlington VT. She died of complic
2 CONC ations from her fourth incidence of cancer.
